{"title":"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Comment_(added_by_pf02,_August_2024)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Comment (added by pf02, August 2024)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a sports contest, there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> medals awarded on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> successive days <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d3e1de014ff843921053d71c34eec61c46e2139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n &gt; 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. On the first day, one medal and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23ff72be03eaa06690b47e6349cade434c034e6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c78c16fe53ddc169da833e13a405ce4988d487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> medals\nwere awarded. On the second day, two medals and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23ff72be03eaa06690b47e6349cade434c034e6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the now remaining\nmedals were awarded; and so on. On the n-th and last day, the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />\nmedals were awarded. How many days did the contest last, and how many\nmedals were awarded altogether?\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is not a particularly elegant solution, but if you start from 1 and go all the way in a clever method, by only guessing those that are 1 more than a multiple of 7, you arrive at the answer of 36.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Comment_.28added_by_pf02.2C_August_2024.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Comment_(added_by_pf02,_August_2024)\">Comment (added by pf02, August 2024)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Comment (added by pf02, August 2024)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Indeed, as the author says, the above is not an elegant solution.  Also,\nit does not give any insight into the uniqueness of the answer to the\nproblem.  I would also comment that choosing to verify the statement\nonly for multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> plus one is not a \"clever method\", it is\nquite an obvious thing to do.  And, note that when the author says\n\"arrive at the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\", they mean \"the contest lasted for\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> medals were awarded\".\n</p><p>Below, I will give another solution, which is more in the spirit and\nstyle of contemporary problem solving.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d8117bc681bc1cb1f9fcbe3f62239c336d0276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_0 = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed417fc2fad9904404efe4ec38ac508d3d64618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of medals left on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />\nafter the medals for the day have been awarded.  The problem says\nthat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bdeebe9ea8f747a18eddab1b77879a5b94c6562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k = m_{k-1} - k - \\frac{m_{k-1} - k}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"39\" /> for\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffef36e8bcacdff85c19dff7173b8707b168368c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, \\dots, (n - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f5a40d8752d842fed264f986f9603fc230b349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{n - 1} = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />.\nSimplify the recursive relation and get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9fe633104dd531f5c8e88e3c9f4bee64eda02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k = \\frac{6}{7}m_{k - 1} - \\frac{6}{7}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We will now get an explicit formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed417fc2fad9904404efe4ec38ac508d3d64618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995bc4c61c81403b083bfcc7d44ce00d8eb61bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1 = \\frac{6}{7}m - \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/527e486f44e089b21620280f549e30c1cc78b057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_2 = \\frac{6}{7}m_1 - \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot 2 = \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^2m - \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^2 \\cdot 1 - \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"382\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60cd4ec998d0076187c7d79a30f2f32836fce6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_3 = \\frac{6}{7}m_2 - \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot 3 = \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^3m - \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^3 \\cdot 1 - \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^2 \\cdot 2 + \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"473\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>. . . . . . . .\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d921a67d921e898b04d8d0ccd434d5dd6833eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{n - 1} = \\frac{6}{7}m_{n - 2} - \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot (n - 1) = \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1}m - \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1} \\cdot 1 - \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 2} \\cdot 2 - \\dots - \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^2 \\cdot (n - 2) - \\frac{6}{7} \\cdot (n - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"842\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>To put it in a shorter way,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/84740dfa149de31f70bf6a0c3a73316ba937cb63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{n - 1} = \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1}m - \\sum_{k = 1}^{n - 1} \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - k} \\cdot k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"292\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>(The reader who is not happy with having obtained this result by having\nobserved the pattern for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed417fc2fad9904404efe4ec38ac508d3d64618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"10\" /> can easily verify it by induction.)\n</p><p>Note that the sum in the equality above is the sum of the arithmetic-geometric\nsequence formed by the geometric progression\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/6872e18416b17ec8a743651dc3e4e7f69888f0d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\ \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1}, \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 2}, \\dots, \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^2, \\frac{6}{7}\\ \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"287\" height=\"48\" />\n(with common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14066033865a9474b53c073a08c70fca00df757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> (note that the progression starts from a\nnumber smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and is increasing)), and the arithmetic progression \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be886298ea80c4bd900c063b3b9575f48be195b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\ 1, 2, \\dots, (n - 2), (n - 1)\\ \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" /> (with common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />).  The\nformula for the sum of the terms of such sequences is reasonably well known\n(and not difficult to prove)\n(see for example <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetico-geometric_series\" title=\"Arithmetico-geometric series\">Arithmetico-geometric_series</a> or\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arithmetico-geometric_sequence\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arithmetico-geometric_sequence</a>).\n</p><p>Applying the formula for the sum of the arithmetic-geometric sequence, and\nusing the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f5a40d8752d842fed264f986f9603fc230b349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{n - 1} = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edba078145c42f663cfa296c6bc4eb19c91fedf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1}m - \\frac{\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1} \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot n}{1 - \\frac{7}{6}} -\\frac{\\frac{7}{6}}{\\left(1 - \\frac{7}{6}\\right)^2} \\left(\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^{n - 1} - 1 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"498\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Now do all the simplifications, and rearrange terms.  We have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/9466754eaa4d0516549e68d92874cad2eec59cca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - 36 = 7(n - 6) \\left(\\frac{7}{6}\\right)^{n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"216\" height=\"48\" /> \n</p><p>In order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> to be an integer, we have to have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d069849e347969a21e7888cca1d88f06bbbc157c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n - 6}{6^{n - 1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> is an integer.  This is clearly\nnot the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/8/b7899a404069a3eccfdf19af391aa0e2a8fcd86f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2, 3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />.  It is an integer\nwhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, in which case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa91a1c9aa24037ad3d0a2bf448bf8e5d8cc7ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.  The fraction is\nnot an integer for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0402efce9f2319988b2f404519983e0e8ff93e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 7$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and even less so for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/7111812e089b5cf31ecc1016f90b56a6b1ca6bcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />\nsince the exponential at the denominator increases much\nfaster than the linear function at the numerator.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2ed1e3c83c78a8baa7ffaa499c04ea8514aaa1c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 36, n = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" /> is the only solution to the problem.\n</p><p>(Solution by pf02, August 2024)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO\" title=\"1967 IMO\">1967 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017165530\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 183/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8538/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.805      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.805      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12080:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017165530 and revision id 233149. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}